Copy-pasted from developer's chat since it might be relevant here.

@dalexeev, thanks for pointing out those comments on the gdscript docs PR! I'm not super certain what to do with it - I think things might be working as intended still. Scripts docs will not be cached (presumably since they can change so often) so will always get processed and returned by the functions that you highlighted.
We could try to start caching them and use some signal in order to keep the caches updated perhaps, but unless we find that is performance-critical it seems like more code for little gain. All of this shows up in `EditorHelpBit` - I'm not entirely sure what it is or where it's used, so it's hard for me to figure out performance details as well.

